{
    include "registries/aaosa_basic.hocon"

    metadata = {
        description = "The planner network. Fires twice per episode: at episode_start it retires last episode's leftover trials, seeds up to 5 new macro trials, and revises the episode plan; at episode_end it judges every trial and closes the episode out.",
        tags = ["maps", "industry", "consultant", "macro", "advisor"],
        sample_queries = [
            "kind=episode_start episode=4 step=0 cumulative_reward=0 final_reward=null",
            "kind=episode_end episode=3 step=100 cumulative_reward=88120 final_reward=88120"
        ]
    },

    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    max_steps = 4000,
    max_execution_seconds = 1200,

    tools = [
        {
            name = "macro_orchestrator",
            function = {
                description = "Front-man router for the planner network. kind=episode_start -> episode_start; kind=episode_end -> episode_end. Does no analysis itself."
            },
            instructions = """
Act as the router for a planner network. For each input, parse its variables and route to the correct function according to these rules:
"kind=<episode_start|episode_end> episode=<E> step=<S> cumulative_reward=<C> final_reward=<F> [recovery=true doom_reason=<...>] [aborted=<true|false> reason=<...>]".

- If `kind=episode_start`:  
  - Call `episode_start` with an inquiry string containing "episode=<E>".
  - If the input contains `recovery=true` and `doom_reason=<...>`, append both tokens verbatim to the inquiry string (e.g. "episode=4 recovery=true doom_reason=<...>").
  - Relay the status line from the planner’s response exactly.

- If `kind=episode_end`:  
  - Call `episode_end(episode=<E>, cumulative_reward=<C>, aborted=<true|false>)`.  
  - If the `aborted` flag is missing, assume `false`.
  - Relay the recap line from the planner’s response exactly.

ERROR HANDLING: if any tool call or downstream agent returns an error, STOP and reply with `ERROR: <the verbatim error text>`.
Never swallow, paraphrase, retry silently, or continue past it.
""",
            middleware = [ {"class": "langchain_anthropic.middleware.AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware", "args": {"ttl": "1h"}} ],
            tools = ["episode_start", "episode_end"]
        },

        {
            name = "episode_start",
            function = ${inquiry_call} {
                description = "Episode-start planner (kind=episode_start). Retires last episode's leftover trials (CarryoverTrials), analyzes best-vs-last, seeds up to 5 macro trials (LogTrial), and revises the plan in place (WriteEpisodePlan: checklist + coordinator strategy summary + per-domain summaries) — keeping what works, changing only what underperformed. Input: episode=<E> [recovery=true doom_reason=<...>]."
            },
            instructions = """
Plan the UPCOMING episode, following every instruction literally, tersely, and without omission.
You are the only part of this harness that can change the multi-agent system's direction. The specialists execute the
plan you write and never reconsider it, so whatever you miss here is repeated for 100 irreversible turns.
No run has ever reached $1M, so a tidier version of the last episode will not get there — the plan that wins is one
nobody has tried yet. Equally, do not throw away what already works: keep the moves the best run proved out, and
spend your novelty where the evidence says the park is failing. Aim high; the gap to $1M is not closed by caution.
Flow: READ prior outcomes → ANALYZE → DECIDE up to 5 TRIALS → LOG them (LogTrial) → REVISE the PLAN for the episode.

RECOVERY MODE: If input includes `recovery=true`, assume last episode failed and playbooks were restored to last champion;
refine this champion with new trial strategies. Use doomed last episode only to identify what to avoid (`doom_reason`).

# Procedure

1. Context — gather all of it before you analyse anything:
    - scratchpad(): the note you left yourself at last episode's close-out.
    - state_read('maps_game_docs'): the complete rules and mechanics.
    - RunTelemetry(select='best_and_last'): per-step performance for the best-ever and the last episode.
    - state_read('status_coordinator') and state_read('status_layout'): LAST EPISODE'S finished park — every
    tier it had unlocked (`available_entities`) and every asset it ended with.
    - state_read('trial_strategies_outcome'): every strategy already attempted, confirmed or falsified, with the
      steer on PRIORITY/DIRECTION.
    - CarryoverTrials(episode=<E>): the trials last episode's close-out left inconclusive. Reading them RETIRES them,
      so one you want to keep or refine must be re-logged in step 4.
    - state_read for every 'playbook_<domain>': the "## Learned rules" promoted by past runs.

2. ANALYZE (THINK OUT OF THE BOX):
    - Treat the best run as your floor, not your target: this episode must build on it and finish ahead of it.
    - Compare the best and last runs move by move. Name where the best pulled ahead, where it stalled, and where the
    last one regressed (pace, research, placements, staff, actions, rejections).
    - Read park_rating after each step to infer what drives rating and how it feeds attendance.
    - Identify the concrete points where a new strategy could beat the current best.
    - Locate the STRUCTURAL BLOCKER, if there is one, and decide the strategy that UNBLOCKS it.

3. Decide up to 5 Trial Strategies:
    - From that analysis, propose up to 5 new, wide-scope, falsifiable strategies aimed at $1M park_value. Use simple detailed language.
    - Keep each one GENERAL — a standing direction for the park, not a rule tied to specific steps or to the exact
    value some variable reaches. "Start research once you have the cash to run it for 3 days" is the right shape;
    "set research to slow at step 31 when min_cleanliness is 0.80" is not.
    - Playbook lines are prior BELIEFS, not physics. Where telemetry contradicts one, the trial is to overturn it —
    name the exact line you are testing against.
    - Never repeat a strategy already falsified or already promoted to the learned rules. Where a carried-over trial
    is still relevant, or could be made relevant by refining it, do that instead of inventing a weaker new one.
    - Work the levers: ride/shop/staff subtypes, the yellow→blue→green→red subclasses, slow/medium/fast research
    speed, and the choice of research topics. A lever the runs have never pulled is your first candidate — an untried
    lever teaches more than a re-tuned one.

4. Log Trials — call LogTrial once for EVERY trial you decided on in step 3, including any carried-over trial you
   chose to keep or refine:
   - new_text: a single imperative command (no numbers or examples), step_start='1'.

5. REVISE THE PLAN — edit the current one, never start from scratch:
   - state_read('episode_checklist'): the phased checklist across turns.
   - state_read('playbook_coordinator'): the current top-level summary.
   - state_read('playbook_<domain>'): read only the domains whose guidance you are changing.
   - RETAIN the phases that performed well. Alter only those that underperformed or that a new trial targets.
   - Call WriteEpisodePlan(checklist_items, strategy_summary, playbook_summaries) with:
     - checklist_items: turns 1-100 covered, one "turns A-B: <goal>" line per phase.
     - strategy_summary: 6-8 phases, each with a goal, a move order and metric targets toward $1M; end with the
       failure modes to avoid.
     - playbook_summaries: 4-5 lines for each domain you changed. Omit the unchanged ones — their current summaries
       are kept.

6. Close — if this episode's close-out must know something, leave it in scratchpad(note=...). It reads the note once
   and it is deleted on that read, so write only what the close-out genuinely needs.

# Error Handling: if any tool call or downstream agent returns an error, STOP and reply with
`ERROR: <the verbatim error text>`. Never paraphrase, retry, ignore, or continue past any error response.
""",
            middleware = [
                {"class": "middleware.trim_history_middleware.TrimHistoryMiddleware", "args": {}}
                {"class": "langchain_anthropic.middleware.AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware", "args": {"ttl": "1h"}}
            ],
            tools = ["RunTelemetry", "state_read", "CarryoverTrials", "LogTrial", "WriteEpisodePlan", "scratchpad"]
        },

        {
            name = "episode_end",
            function = ${inquiry_call} {
                description = "Episode-end close-out (kind=episode_end). Judges every active trial on its own evidence — an aborted run included — promotes the confirmed ones, then ResolveTrials and advance_episode. Inputs: episode, cumulative_reward, aborted."
            },
            instructions = """
You are responsible for the end-of-episode close-out and playbook rule-writing.

This episode cost 100 irreversible turns, and nobody reads it again — whatever the system learns from it,
you extract here. A confirmed trial becomes a playbook rule the park obeys forever, surviving even a fresh start,
so every verdict you get wrong costs something the project never gets back.

- CONFIRM one that deserved falsifying — the park is aimed at a wrong strategy for every run to come,
  and never performs at its best however well the specialists execute.
- FALSIFY one that deserved confirming — that direction is shut for good, the domain never explored again.
- Leave one INCONCLUSIVE — it passes to the next planner as unfinished business,
  taking a slot a sharper idea could have had.

So read this evidence harshly, in both directions. A falsified trial is worth as much as a confirmed one —
it permanently removes a dead end — but only the telemetry decides which you are holding.
Judge on what the run shows and the park compounds.

Always use evidence from EpisodeTelemetry. Never invent or assume data. Use the provided tools effectively.

# Procedure
1. Get context as needed:
   - scratchpad() — the note the planner network left at its last run (usually this episode's start plan).
   Reading CLEARS it. Empty means nothing was left. Whatever it names is what you must settle in this close-out.
   - state_read('last_reward') — prior episode’s reward (or 0)
   - ActiveTrials() — trials you must evaluate this close-out
   - EpisodeTelemetry() — step-by-step telemetry and rejections
   - state_read('status_coordinator') and state_read('status_layout') — THIS EPISODE'S finished park — every
    tier it had unlocked (`available_entities`) and every asset it ended with, to analyze it.
2. For each active trial (even if the run is doomed):
    - Check whether the intended action fired by reading the run itself: EpisodeTelemetry().steps carries the full
    action args (incl. x/y) plus per-step metrics, and .rejections lists what the sim refused.
    - Judge per trial:
        - success on the decided metric AND no failure: confirmed
        - failure: falsified
        - neither: inconclusive
3. For confirmed trials: PromoteTrial(domain, edit_type='add_line', new_text=<imperative, general, one sentence>, episode=<E>, section='Learned rules (promoted from prior runs)'). Only append lines.
4. Finish trials: ResolveTrials(episode=<E>, report=<per-trial [{trial_id, domain, outcome, note}]>).
5. Close the books: advance_episode(final_reward=<C>, episode=<E>).
6. Output: One short line: "<N> promoted, <M> falsified, final=<C>" (and mention if aborted).
This will appear in the next episode’s prompt—be concise.
7. LAST: if the planner's NEXT run (the next episode's start plan) must know something, call scratchpad.

# Error Handling: If any tool call or downstream agent returns an error, STOP and reply with `ERROR: <the verbatim error text>`
Never paraphrase, retry, ignore, or continue past any error response.

# Notes
- Never invent or assume results—always use direct telemetry and tool evidence.
- Do not modify, paraphrase, or retry on errors.
- Keep every action and output as short and formal as possible.
""",
            middleware = [
                {"class": "middleware.trim_history_middleware.TrimHistoryMiddleware", "args": {}},
                {"class": "langchain_anthropic.middleware.AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware", "args": {"ttl": "1h"}}
            ],
            tools = ["state_read", "EpisodeTelemetry", "ActiveTrials", "PromoteTrial", "ResolveTrials", "advance_episode", "scratchpad"]
        },

        {
            name = "scratchpad",
            class = "coded_tools.scratchpad.Scratchpad",
            function = {
                description = "Private memo for this network; player and watcher hold their own. episode_start and episode_end share it, chaining start -> end -> next start. No args reads and clears the previous run's note; note=<text> leaves up to 5 lines for the next run. Writes replace; no history is kept.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        note = {
                            type = "string",
                            description = "Up to 5 lines to carry into the planner's NEXT run only. Omit to read-and-clear instead."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            args = { pad = "planner" }
        },

        {
            name = "advance_episode",
            class = "coded_tools.advance_episode.AdvanceEpisode",
            function = {
                description = "End-of-episode bookkeeping: persists the final reward and clears the observation cache. The outcome ledger is append-only — every episode's OUTCOME lines are kept for the whole run. No prose summary is stored — the OUTCOME lines ResolveTrials wrote are the record. Trial cleanup is not done here — CarryoverTrials handles it at the next episode start.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        final_reward = {
                            type = "float",
                            description = "This episode's cumulative_reward; written to last_reward.md."
                        },
                        episode = {
                            type = "int",
                            description = "Current episode number; bounds which OUTCOME lines are kept."
                        },
                    },
                    required = ["final_reward", "episode"]
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "RunTelemetry",
            class = "coded_tools.run_telemetry.RunTelemetry",
            function = {
                description = "Cross-episode telemetry in three modes. SELECT (select='best_and_last') returns the best-ever and the last episode as raw per-step rows, unaggregated — use this to read the moves themselves. RUNS (num_runs, default 5) returns per-run and per-episode rollups for the N most recent runs, plus a cross-run rollup. EPISODE (default) returns per-episode rollups for the current run, including reward_bands: mean reward per step over turns 1-25, 26-50, 51-75 and 76-100.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        select = { type = "string", description = "SELECT mode: pass 'best_and_last' for the best-ever and the last episode as raw per-step rows, unaggregated." }
                        num_runs = { type = "int", description = "RUNS mode: analyze the N most recent runs (current + prior). Default 5." }
                        scope = { type = "string", description = "Optional explicit mode: 'select', 'runs', or 'episodes'. Usually leave unset — select/num_runs select the mode." }
                        from_episode = { type = "int", description = "EPISODE mode only: include episodes >= this. Omit for the whole current run." }
                        max_episodes = { type = "int", description = "EPISODE mode only: keep only the most recent N episodes (after from_episode). Omit for all." }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "WriteEpisodePlan",
            class = "coded_tools.write_episode_plan.WriteEpisodePlan",
            function = {
                description = "Persists the episode plan, overwriting the previous one: the turn-phased checklist (episode_checklist.md, source of current_phase), the coordinator's strategy summary (playbook_coordinator.md, read every turn), and optional per-domain summaries in the rides/shops/staff/research/layout/survey playbooks.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        checklist_items = {
                            type = "array",
                            items = { type = "string" },
                            description = "The full turn-phased plan, one literal 'turns A-B: <goal>' line per item, ordered by turn, covering turns 1..100."
                        }
                        strategy_summary = {
                            type = "string",
                            description = "Prose brief giving the reasoning behind the checklist: 6-8 phases, each with a goal, a move order and metric targets, closing with the failure modes to avoid. Written into playbook_coordinator, which strategy_coordinator reads every turn."
                        }
                        playbook_summaries = {
                            type = "object",
                            description = "Optional per-domain summaries, keyed by 'rides','shops','staff','research','layout' or 'survey'. Each value is a 4-5 line brief on how that specialist should play THIS episode, drawn from the best-vs-last comparison; it is written to the top of that specialist's playbook and read on every consultation. Omit a domain to leave its current summary unchanged.",
                            properties = {
                                rides    = { type = "string", description = "4-5 line summary for rides_manager this episode." }
                                shops    = { type = "string", description = "4-5 line summary for shops_manager this episode." }
                                staff    = { type = "string", description = "4-5 line summary for staffing_manager this episode." }
                                research = { type = "string", description = "4-5 line summary for research_lead this episode." }
                                layout   = { type = "string", description = "4-5 line summary for park_layout_planner this episode." }
                                survey   = { type = "string", description = "4-5 line summary for guest_analyst this episode." }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    required = ["checklist_items", "strategy_summary"]
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "EpisodeTelemetry",
            class = "coded_tools.episode_telemetry.EpisodeTelemetry",
            function = {
                description = "Per-step record for ONE episode, read from run.jsonl: {steps, rejections, rollup}, exists=false before any row is written. Each step carries its full action args and metrics. Judge whether a trial's move fired from `steps` and `rejections`, and its success from the per-step reward/value/rating deltas. `rejections` records every action the sim refused, booked as a wait with the original action and error; the same rejection repeating is a prime trial target.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        episode   = { type = "int", description = "Episode number to read. Omit to use the latest episode present in the log." }
                        from_step = { type = "int", description = "Only return steps >= this (mid-episode tail). Omit for the full episode." }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "LogTrial",
            class = "coded_tools.log_trial.LogTrial",
            function = {
                description = "Mints a collision-free trial_id and appends the paired lines: the one-line rule to trial_strategies, the metadata and success/failure criteria to trial_strategies_criteria. Use it for every new trial: it owns id minting and criteria formatting, and takes origin from this network's config.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        episode           = { type = "int", description = "Current episode number." }
                        step_start        = { type = "string",  description = "Step at which the trial activates (as a string), or the literal 'end_of_episode'." }
                        domain            = { type = "string",  description = "One of: rides, shops, staff, research, layout, survey, coordinator." }
                        section           = { type = "string",  description = "Target playbook section header (or 'new')." }
                        edit_type         = { type = "string",  description = "'add_line' or 'replace_line'." }
                        new_text          = { type = "string",  description = "The one-line rule to add/replace (no rationale or metrics embedded)." }
                        find_text         = { type = "string",  description = "replace_line only: the exact existing playbook line to replace." }
                        rationale         = { type = "string",  description = "One sentence citing step(s) / metric delta." }
                        success_criterion = { type = "string",  description = "Observable metric + direction + evaluation window (turns; fits in the fixed 100-step episode)." }
                        failure_criterion = { type = "string",  description = "Observable metric that would falsify the trial." }
                    }
                    required = ["episode", "step_start", "domain", "section", "edit_type", "new_text", "rationale", "success_criterion", "failure_criterion"]
                }
            }
            args = { origin = "macro" }
        },

        {
            name = "ActiveTrials",
            class = "coded_tools.active_trials.ActiveTrials",
            function = {
                description = "Return the active trials joined across trial_strategies (rule body) and trial_strategies_criteria (metadata), optionally filtered by domain and/or trial_origin ('micro'|'macro').",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        domain = { type = "string", description = "Filter to one domain: rides, shops, staff, research, layout, survey or coordinator. Omit for all domains." }
                        trial_origin = { type = "string", description = "Filter to 'micro' or 'macro'; omit for both. Named trial_origin, not origin — the framework injects a reserved 'origin' key that would silently override it." }
                    }
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "CarryoverTrials",
            class = "coded_tools.carryover_trials.CarryoverTrials",
            function = {
                description = "Episode-start tool. Returns the trials left over from earlier episodes — the ones the last close-out left inconclusive — and retires them in the same call, recording an OUTCOME line with the rule text for each. A leftover therefore informs exactly one planning pass; re-log any you want to keep. Scoped to earlier episodes, so trials logged for the episode being planned stay active and the call is safe in any order.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        episode = { type = "int", description = "The episode being planned. Trials from EARLIER episodes are returned and cleared." }
                    }
                    required = ["episode"]
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "ResolveTrials",
            class = "coded_tools.resolve_trials.ResolveTrials",
            function = {
                description = "Applies the per-trial report at episode end. Confirmed and falsified trials are removed from trial_strategies and trial_strategies_criteria; not_applied and inconclusive are kept for the next planner, as is any active trial absent from the report (recorded inconclusive, note='no_report'). Every MACRO trial gets an OUTCOME line, carrying its rule text, in trial_strategies_outcome; micro trials are episode-scoped and are dropped without a line.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        episode = { type = "int", description = "Current episode number." }
                        report  = { type = "string", description = "JSON list of the curator's per-trial objects: [{trial_id, domain, outcome, note}], outcome in confirmed/falsified/not_applied/inconclusive." }
                    }
                    required = ["episode", "report"]
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "PromoteTrial",
            class = "coded_tools.promote_trial.PromoteTrial",
            function = {
                description = "Applies ONE confirmed trial's edit to playbook_<domain>.md, tagging the line '(learned ep<N>)'. add_line appends at the end (section 'end'/'new'/empty) or after the named section header; replace_line replaces the unique find_text. A successful edit is mirrored into config_files/seed_playbook_<domain>.md under '## Learned rules', so the rule survives a fresh run.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        domain    = { type = "string",  description = "rides/shops/staff/research/layout/survey/coordinator." }
                        edit_type = { type = "string",  description = "'add_line' or 'replace_line'." }
                        new_text  = { type = "string",  description = "The rule line to add/replace (without the learned tag)." }
                        episode   = { type = "int", description = "Episode number for the '(learned ep<N>)' tag." }
                        section   = { type = "string",  description = "add_line: section header to insert after, or 'end'/'new' to append." }
                        find_text = { type = "string",  description = "replace_line: the exact existing playbook line to replace." }
                    }
                    required = ["domain", "edit_type", "new_text", "episode"]
                }
            }
        },

        {
            name = "state_read",
            class = "coded_tools.state_read.StateRead",
            function = {
                description = "Read a file by its logical name from the operator-configured name_map.",
                parameters = {
                    type = "object",
                    properties = {
                        name = { type = "string", description = "Logical name of the file to read; must be one the operator mapped in name_map." }
                    },
                    required = ["name"]
                }
            },
            args = {
                name_map = {
                    # The park as LAST EPISODE LEFT IT. Both planner passes run before
                    # the runner's next ParkStatus refresh, so these hold the final
                    # pre-reset snapshot of the episode being reviewed — never the new
                    # park. Telemetry rows carry aggregates only (num_rides, park_value)
                    # and can never name WHICH asset ended up the drag.
                    status_coordinator          = "coded_tools/state/status_coordinator.json"
                    status_layout               = "coded_tools/state/status_layout.json"
                    trial_strategies            = "coded_tools/state/trial_strategies.md"
                    trial_strategies_criteria   = "coded_tools/state/trial_strategies_criteria.md"
                    trial_strategies_outcome    = "coded_tools/state/trial_strategies_outcome.md"
                    last_reward                 = "coded_tools/state/last_reward.md"
                    playbook_coordinator        = "coded_tools/state/playbook_coordinator.md"
                    playbook_rides              = "coded_tools/state/playbook_rides.md"
                    playbook_shops              = "coded_tools/state/playbook_shops.md"
                    playbook_staff              = "coded_tools/state/playbook_staff.md"
                    playbook_research           = "coded_tools/state/playbook_research.md"
                    playbook_layout             = "coded_tools/state/playbook_layout.md"
                    playbook_survey             = "coded_tools/state/playbook_survey.md"
                    episode_checklist           = "coded_tools/state/episode_checklist.md"
                    economics_rides             = "coded_tools/config_files/economics_rides.md"
                    economics_shops             = "coded_tools/config_files/economics_shops.md"
                    economics_staff             = "coded_tools/config_files/economics_staff.md"
                    economics_research          = "coded_tools/config_files/economics_research.md"
                    maps_game_docs              = "coded_tools/config_files/maps_game_docs.md"
                    seed_playbook_coordinator   = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_coordinator.md"
                    seed_playbook_rides         = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_rides.md"
                    seed_playbook_shops         = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_shops.md"
                    seed_playbook_staff         = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_staff.md"
                    seed_playbook_research      = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_research.md"
                    seed_playbook_layout        = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_layout.md"
                    seed_playbook_survey        = "coded_tools/config_files/seed_playbook_survey.md"
                }
            }
        },
    ]
}
